    <bpmn:process id="W_W680" name="W680. Supply Chain Cost Analysis &amp; Logistics Optimization Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly cost analysis cycle; quarterly optimization review
Frequency: Monthly cost analysis; quarterly optimization review; annual strategic assessment
Volume: ~PHP 3-4B annual supply chain cost (inbound freight, DC operations, outbound distribution, 3PL, port/customs); ~600,000 store replenishment orders/year (production-calibrated per data-volumes §1.1)
Owner: VP Supply Chain
Participants: DC Operations Manager, Logistics Manager, FP&amp;A Analyst, Procurement Manager
Source: workflow W680 — Supply Chain Cost Analysis &amp; Logistics Optimization Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W680_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W680_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W680_Lane2" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W680_Lane3" name="DC Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W680_Lane4" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W680_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W680_Start6" name="Monthly cost analysis cycle; quarterly optimization review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W680_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W680_Task7" name="FP&amp;A Analyst extracts monthly supply chain cost data from GL: inbound freight…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: FP&amp;A Analyst extracts monthly supply chain cost data from GL: inbound freight (vendor-to-DC), import logistics (port/customs/brokerage per W464), DC operating costs (labor, equipment, utilities per W584), outbound distribution (DC-to-store, 3PL per W242), inter-island freight (W66), last-mile delivery (W268), and fleet costs (W198 fuel + W199 telematics)
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W680_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W680_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W680_Task8" name="VP Supply Chain reviews cost-per-unit metrics: cost per case received, cost per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VP Supply Chain reviews cost-per-unit metrics: cost per case received, cost per case shipped, cost per store delivery, cost per ecommerce order fulfilled, cost per TEU imported; compares against prior month, same period last year, and industry benchmarks
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W680_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W680_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W680_Task9" name="DC Operations Manager provides DC cost analysis: labor cost per unit handled…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: DC Operations Manager provides DC cost analysis: labor cost per unit handled (receiving, putaway, picking, shipping), equipment cost per hour, facility cost per sqm, overtime as % of total DC labor; identifies cost reduction opportunities
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W680_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W680_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W680_Task10" name="Logistics Manager analyzes distribution cost: owned fleet vs. 3PL cost per km…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Logistics Manager analyzes distribution cost: owned fleet vs. 3PL cost per km per kg, route efficiency (deliveries per route, utilization rate per W196), fuel cost per delivery (per W198), port demurrage avoidance per W249
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W680_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W680_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W680_Task11" name="VP Supply Chain identifies optimization opportunities: DC network rebalancing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: VP Supply Chain identifies optimization opportunities: DC network rebalancing (can any DC serve more stores with shorter routes), consolidation opportunities (combining shipments to reduce truck count), mode shift evaluation (DSD vs. DC fulfillment for specific categories), 3PL contract renegotiation per W242
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W680_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W680_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W680_Task12" name="Monthly: VP Supply Chain produces cost trend dashboard for COO: total supply…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly: VP Supply Chain produces cost trend dashboard for COO: total supply chain cost as % of revenue (target ≤ 6%), per-unit cost trends, and top 3 cost reduction initiatives in progress
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W680_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W680_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W680_Task13" name="Quarterly: VP Supply Chain conducts optimization review with COO and CFO…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly: VP Supply Chain conducts optimization review with COO and CFO: presents cost reduction roadmap, capital investment proposals (e.g., DC automation, fleet replacement), and make-vs-buy analysis for logistics
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO, CFO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W680_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W680_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W680_Task14" name="Annual: VP Supply Chain develops 3-year logistics strategy aligned with store…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Annual: VP Supply Chain develops 3-year logistics strategy aligned with store expansion plan (10-15 new stores/year): DC capacity planning, fleet sizing, 3PL partner strategy, and technology roadmap
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO, CFO
Duration: 5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W680_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W680_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W680_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W680_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W680_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-245 (ensure controlled execution — Supply Chain Orchestration &amp; Risk (PA-02.3).) | - operational: VP Supply Chain review and approval gate
Owner: VP Supply Chain</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W680_Assoc17" sourceRef="W680_Annotation16" targetRef="W680_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
