    <bpmn:process id="W_W1031" name="W1031. Customer Delivery Service Area Geo-Fencing &amp; Coverage Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store opening; periodic zone review (quarterly); customer address validation at checkout
Frequency: Quarterly review × 200 stores; real-time validation at every delivery order
Volume: 200 delivery zones; ~42,900 ecommerce orders/month + ~5,000–8,000 in-store delivery orders/month
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager
Participants: Supply Chain Planner, Store Manager, 3PL Partner Manager, IT GIS Analyst
Source: workflow W1031 — Customer Delivery Service Area Geo-Fencing &amp; Coverage Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1031_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1031_Lane1" name="IT GIS Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1031_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1031_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1031_Lane2" name="Ecommerce Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1031_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1031_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1031_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1031_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1031_Lane4" name="Supply Chain Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1031_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1031_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1031_Start6" name="New store opening; periodic zone review (quarterly); customer address validation at…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1031_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1031_Task7" name="Zone Boundary Definition &amp; GIS Mapping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Zone Boundary Definition &amp; GIS Mapping: IT GIS Analyst defines delivery zones for each store: (a) Zone 1 (Core): 0–5 km radius from store; delivery SLA: same-day or next-day; delivery fee: PHP 99 or free above PHP 5,000; coverage: urban barangays within easy driving distance; polygon drawn on GIS map considering natural boundaries (rivers, highways, gated communities); (b) Zone 2 (Standard): 5–15 km radius; delivery SLA: 1–2 business days; delivery fee: PHP 199 or free above PHP 8,000; (c) Zone 3 (Extended): 15–30 km radius; delivery SLA: 2–3 business days; delivery fee: PHP 350+ based on distance; (d) Zone 4 (Remote/DC-fulfilled): 30+ km from nearest store; delivery SLA: 3–5 business days; fulfillment from nearest DC; delivery fee: PHP 500+ based on distance and weight; (e) Excluded areas: areas unreachable by standard vehicles (island barangays without bridge access, mountain roads impassable during rainy season) — customer redirected to BOPIS (W11) or smart locker (W247); (f) zones defined as GIS polygons (not simple radius circles) to account for road network, natural barriers, and 3PL partner coverage areas
Responsible (R): IT GIS Analyst / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours per store (initial setup); 2–3 hours per store (quarterly update)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1031_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1031_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1031_Task8" name="3PL Partner Coverage Mapping">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: 3PL Partner Coverage Mapping: Ecommerce Operations Manager maps 3PL partner capabilities per zone: (a) Lalamove: strong coverage in Metro Manila, Cebu, and Davao urban areas; motorcycle and car for small-medium items; limited for bulky items (lumber, cement); (b) Transportify: covers wider geographic area including provincial routes; van and truck options for bulky items; (c) Own fleet (BuildRight Logistics): 10-wheeler wing vans for DC-to-store and large B2B deliveries; limited availability for B2C last-mile; (d) local provincial transporters: contracted per region for areas outside 3PL coverage; (e) system stores 3PL partner-zone mapping: which carrier serves which zone, at what cost, with what vehicle type, and SLA; (f) when multiple carriers serve the same zone, system selects based on: cost optimization, vehicle availability, SLA compliance history per W1013
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Operations Manager / 3PL Partner Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 8–12 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1031_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1031_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1031_Task9" name="Real-Time Address Validation &amp; Zone Assignment at Checkout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Real-Time Address Validation &amp; Zone Assignment at Checkout: Customer places delivery order on buildright.com.ph or in-store: (a) customer enters delivery address; system geocodes address to GPS coordinates using PSA PSGC hierarchy (MDM-019) and Google Maps API; (b) system matches GPS coordinates against zone GIS polygons; (c) if address falls within a defined zone: (i) system displays delivery SLA and fee for that zone, (ii) assigns fulfillment location (nearest store or DC) based on zone mapping, (iii) customer sees &quot;Delivery available: 1–2 business days, PHP 199&quot;; (d) if address falls outside all zones (excluded area): (i) system displays &quot;Home delivery not available for this address. Would you like to pick up at [nearest store]? (BOPIS available)&quot;, (ii) customer redirected to BOPIS flow per W11; (e) if address geocoding fails (ambiguous Philippine address): (i) system prompts customer to add landmark and nearest major road, (ii) manual zone assignment by customer service agent within 2 hours for orders with failed geocoding
Responsible (R): System / Customer Service Agent
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: &lt; 10 sec (automated); 5–10 min (manual override)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1031_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1031_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1031_Task10" name="Zone Conflict Resolution &amp; Store Overlap Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Zone Conflict Resolution &amp; Store Overlap Management: When two stores&#x27; zones overlap: (a) system assigns order to store with: (i) shortest driving distance to delivery address (via Google Maps routing API), (ii) best in-stock position for ordered items (ATP check), (iii) lowest delivery cost (considering 3PL vs. own fleet); (b) tiebreaker: store with lower current fulfillment workload (balanced workload distribution); (c) DM can override zone assignment in exceptional cases (e.g., one store is temporarily out of a critical item); (d) monthly: system generates zone overlap analysis — identify orders where a different fulfillment store would have been more cost-effective; optimize zone boundaries accordingly
Responsible (R): System / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1031_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1031_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1031_Task11" name="Quarterly Zone Review &amp; New Store Integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly Zone Review &amp; New Store Integration: Quarterly zone review: (a) analyze delivery performance per zone: SLA compliance rate, delivery cost per order, customer complaint rate for delivery; (b) identify underperforming zones: high SLA breach rate → re-evaluate carrier assignment or adjust SLA; high cost → optimize route or renegotiate 3PL rates; (c) adjust zone boundaries based on: new road infrastructure, 3PL coverage expansion, population growth areas; (d) new store integration: when a new store opens per W16 (New Store Opening): (i) new store&#x27;s zones carved from adjacent stores&#x27; zones (step 1), (ii) existing orders in transition period rerouted to new store, (iii) affected customers notified of new closer delivery option; (e) update GIS polygons, 3PL partner mapping, and system configuration
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Planner / IT GIS Analyst
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 8–12 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1031_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1031_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1031_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1031_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1031_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-245 (ensure controlled execution — Supply Chain Orchestration &amp; Risk (PA-02.3).) | - operational: must support temporary zone suspension with customer notification
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1031_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1031_Annotation13" targetRef="W1031_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1031_Flow15" sourceRef="W1031_Start6" targetRef="W1031_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1031_Flow16" sourceRef="W1031_Task7" targetRef="W1031_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1031_Flow17" sourceRef="W1031_Task8" targetRef="W1031_Task9" />
