    <bpmn:process id="W_W1187" name="W1187. Post-Disaster Construction Material Demand Surge Fulfillment &amp; Emergency Replenishment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA typhoon signal lowered to Storm Signal No. 1 or below; or regional disaster declaration by NDRRMC / LGU
Frequency: ~3–5 major events/year (typhoons, flooding); localized flooding more frequent in low-lying areas
Volume: 200–400% demand surge on roofing, plywood, nails, cement, waterproofing, and tarpaulins in affected regions for 2–4 weeks post-event
Owner: VP Supply Chain
Participants: VP Supply Chain, Supply Planner, DC Supervisor, Category Managers (Lumber, Plumbing, Paint), Logistics Manager, Purchasing Manager, Store Managers (affected region)
Source: workflow W1187 — Post-Disaster Construction Material Demand Surge Fulfillment &amp; Emergency Replenishment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1187_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1187_Lane1" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1187_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1187_Lane3" name="Purchasing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1187_Lane4" name="Logistics Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1187_Lane5" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1187_Lane6" name="Supply Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1187_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1187_Start8" name="PAGASA typhoon signal lowered to Storm Signal No. 1 or below; or regional disaster…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1187_Task9" name="Disaster alert activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Disaster alert activation: Upon PAGASA Signal No. 2 or higher for any region, VP Supply Chain activates &quot;Disaster Response Mode&quot; in ERP; system flags all stores within affected provinces; pre-positioned disaster SKU list (50–80 SKUs: roofing GI sheets, plywood, nails, cement, tarpaulins, waterproofing sealant, lumber) is automatically loaded
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1187_Task10" name="Demand surge estimation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Demand surge estimation: System calculates estimated demand surge using historical post-disaster sales patterns (3–5x normal for roofing, 2–3x for cement, 4–6x for tarpaulins) applied to affected store count and baseline demand; generates emergency replenishment quantities per SKU per store
Responsible (R): System / Supply Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1187_Task11" name="DC inventory allocation sweep">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: DC inventory allocation sweep: System sweeps available inventory across all 4 DCs for disaster SKUs; allocates available stock to affected stores by priority (highest-damage zones first); flags shortfalls for emergency procurement
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1187_Task12" name="Emergency procurement activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Emergency procurement activation: For shortfalls identified in Step 3: Purchasing Manager contacts top 20 vendors for disaster SKUs via emergency PO; negotiates expedited production and delivery; issues emergency POs with shortened lead time targets (local: 3–5 days vs. normal 7–21 days); activates backup vendors per W921 if primary vendors are also affected
Responsible (R): Purchasing Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1187_Task13" name="Inter-DC emergency transfer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Inter-DC emergency transfer: If one DC is incapacitated or depleted, VP Supply Chain authorizes emergency inter-DC transfers from unaffected DCs per W22 (inter-DC transfers); Logistics Manager arranges expedited long-haul transport (e.g., Davao → Manila if Luzon DCs affected)
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain / Logistics Mgr
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1187_Task14" name="Store delivery prioritization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Store delivery prioritization: Logistics Manager re-prioritizes DC outbound delivery schedule; disaster replenishment orders get highest dispatch priority; stores in affected areas receive daily deliveries (vs. normal 2–3x/week); system auto-adjusts route plans
Responsible (R): Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1187_Task15" name="Price freeze compliance check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Price freeze compliance check: VP Legal &amp; Compliance confirms if DTI / LGU has imposed a price freeze on construction materials under RA 7581 (Price Act); if yes, system locks SRP for affected SKUs in affected regions; any promotional markdowns on disaster SKUs are suspended
Responsible (R): VP Legal
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1187_Task16" name="Hourly dashboard monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Hourly dashboard monitoring: During the first 72 hours post-disaster, Supply Planner monitors real-time sell-through rates for disaster SKUs via control tower dashboard (W250); compares actual demand surge vs. estimated; triggers additional procurement if actual exceeds estimate by &gt; 20%
Responsible (R): Supply Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Continuous (72h)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1187_Task17" name="Gradual de-escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Gradual de-escalation: As demand normalizes (typically 2–4 weeks post-event), VP Supply Chain gradually de-escalates from Disaster Response Mode; normal replenishment parameters resume; emergency PO commitments are fulfilled; excess inventory from over-procurement is rebalanced across unaffected stores per W22
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Weekly review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1187_Task18" name="Post-event review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Post-event review: Within 30 days, VP Supply Chain conducts post-disaster supply chain review: (a) actual vs. estimated demand surge by SKU, (b) DC response time, (c) vendor emergency fulfillment rate, (d) stockout rate during surge period, (e) inter-DC transfer effectiveness; findings update disaster playbook parameters
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1187_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1187_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1187_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1187_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-245 (ensure controlled execution — Supply Chain Orchestration &amp; Risk (PA-02.3).) | - operational: pre-negotiated emergency supply agreements with vendors outside typhoon-prone regions; operational: maintaining 2-week safety stock buffers at each DC for disaster SKUs during typhoon season (Jun–Nov); operational: automated price lock mechanism in Step 7
Owner: VP Supply Chain</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
