    <bpmn:process id="W_W1432" name="W1432. Store-Level Typhoon Season Advance Inventory Pre-Positioning, Protective Stocking &amp; Post-Storm Rapid Replenishment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA typhoon advisory (Signal 1 or higher approaching BuildRight store regions); or annual typhoon season preparedness review (May, before rainy season)
Frequency: Annual preparedness planning (May); active response 10–15 typhoon events per year affecting BuildRight store regions; post-storm replenishment as needed (estimated 3–5 significant events/year requiring rapid replenishment)
Volume: ~40 stores in typhoon-prone Visayas region + ~50 stores in Luzon typhoon corridor = ~90 stores at elevated typhoon risk (per profile §2 regional split); post-storm rapid replenishment: ~20–30 stores per significant event, each requiring emergency delivery of high-demand items
Owner: Supply Planning Manager
Participants: Supply Planning Manager, DC Supervisor, Logistics Coordinator, Store Manager, VP Store Operations, VP Merchandising, Category Manager (Building Materials)
Source: workflow W1432 — Store-Level Typhoon Season Advance Inventory Pre-Positioning, Protective Stocking &amp; Post-Storm Rapid Replenishment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1432_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1432_Lane1" name="Supply Planning Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1432_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1432_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1432_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1432_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1432_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1432_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1432_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1432_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1432_Start4" name="PAGASA typhoon advisory (Signal 1 or higher approaching BuildRight store regions); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1432_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1432_Task5" name="Annual typhoon season pre-positioning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual typhoon season pre-positioning (May, before rainy season): (a) Supply Planning Manager reviews historical typhoon demand patterns: (i) top 20 post-typhoon items by volume and revenue (typically: plywood, G.I. sheets, cement, nails, tarpaulins, waterproofing, electrical wire, PVC pipes, paint, lumber), (ii) demand multiplier: post-typhoon demand for these items is typically 3–5× normal demand in affected stores, (b) pre-position inventory at DCs: (i) increase safety stock for top 20 typhoon items at DC2 (Cebu) and DC3 (Calamba) — the DCs serving the most typhoon-prone regions, (ii) advance import orders for items sourced internationally (plywood, G.I. sheets) to arrive before typhoon season, (c) VP Merchandising pre-negotiates with key vendors for emergency supply agreements: guaranteed allocation during post-typhoon demand surge
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1432_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1432_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1432_Task6" name="Event-specific protective stocking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Event-specific protective stocking (when PAGASA issues typhoon warning): (a) Supply Planning Manager activates event-specific response: (i) identify stores in projected typhoon path using PAGASA track forecast, (ii) for stores in the path: push emergency delivery of top 20 typhoon items (if DC has stock and roads are still passable — typically 24–48 hours before landfall), (iii) for stores outside the path but near enough to receive evacuees: increase stock of emergency supplies (tarpaulins, flashlights, batteries, water containers), (b) Store Manager executes protective measures per W1221 (typhoon preparation): (i) move outdoor lumber yard inventory indoors or secure with tarps and tie-downs, (ii) elevate bottom-shelf merchandise (flood risk), (iii) stage sandbags at entry points
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–8 hours per typhoon event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1432_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1432_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1432_Task7" name="Post-storm damage assessment and demand estimation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Post-storm damage assessment and demand estimation (within 24 hours of typhoon passage): (a) Store Managers report store status: (i) store damage (structural, flooding, inventory loss), (ii) store operational status (open/closed, operating hours), (iii) local community damage assessment (residential damage drives reconstruction demand), (b) Supply Planning Manager estimates post-storm demand: (i) based on historical post-typhoon patterns × community damage severity, (ii) identify which stores will see reconstruction demand spike, (iii) prioritize replenishment: stores in hardest-hit areas first
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1432_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1432_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1432_Task8" name="Rapid replenishment execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Rapid replenishment execution (T+1 to T+14 days): (a) Supply Planning Manager creates emergency replenishment orders: (i) top 20 typhoon items in 3–5× normal quantities for affected stores, (ii) DC Supervisor prioritizes emergency picks over routine replenishment, (b) Logistics Coordinator arranges emergency transport: (i) assess road conditions (some roads may be impassable), (ii) deploy additional trucks from third-party logistics partners if own fleet is insufficient, (iii) coordinate with LGU for road clearance priority (BuildRight may receive priority as essential goods supplier), (c) Store Manager manages post-storm selling: (i) extended operating hours if community needs, (ii) potential price gouging scrutiny per Consumer Act (RA 7394) — BuildRight must maintain SRP for essential reconstruction materials during declared calamities
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager / DC Supervisor / Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 7–14 days per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1432_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1432_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1432_Task9" name="Post-season review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-season review (November, after typhoon season): (a) Supply Planning Manager conducts post-season typhoon response review: (i) number of typhoon events and stores affected, (ii) pre-positioning accuracy: were the right items pre-stocked?, (iii) replenishment speed: how quickly were affected stores re-stocked?, (iv) lost sales estimate: revenue missed due to stockouts during/after typhoons, (v) inventory damage: total inventory lost to typhoon damage (insurance claims per W853), (b) update typhoon response playbook for next season
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1432_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1432_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1432_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1432_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1432_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-245 (ensure controlled execution — Supply Chain Orchestration &amp; Risk (PA-02.3).) | - operational: Supply Planning Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Supply Planning Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1432_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1432_Annotation11" targetRef="W1432_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1432_Flow13" sourceRef="W1432_Start4" targetRef="W1432_Task5" />
