      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1435" name="W1435. Import Container Consolidation Optimization, Carrier Space Allocation &amp; Port Congestion Mitigation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Weekly import planning cycle; or container space availability alert from freight forwarder
Frequency: Weekly planning; daily monitoring during peak import season (Sep–Dec ber-months and Mar–Apr summer construction season)
Volume: ~400–600 TEUs/month across all import vendors; ~45–70 FCL containers/week (predominantly 40&#x27; HQ) requiring port processing
Owner: Import &amp; Customs Manager
Participants: Import &amp; Customs Manager, Logistics Coordinator, Category Managers (import categories), Freight Forwarder Partners, Customs Broker
Source: workflow W1435 — Import Container Consolidation Optimization, Carrier Space Allocation &amp; Port Congestion Mitigation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1435_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1435_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1435_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1435_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1435_Lane2" name="Import Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1435_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1435_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1435_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1435_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1435_Lane3" name="Freight Forwarder">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1435_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1435_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1435_Start5" name="Weekly import planning cycle; or container space availability alert from freight forwarder">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1435_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1435_Task6" name="Weekly import container demand consolidation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly import container demand consolidation: System aggregates all open import POs with expected ship dates in the next 2–4 weeks; group by origin port, destination port, and commodity type; calculate total CBM and weight per shipment group
Responsible (R): System / Import Manager
Accountable (A): Import Manager
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1435_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1435_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1435_Task7" name="Container utilization optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Container utilization optimization: Import Manager reviews consolidation opportunities: (a) combine partial-container shipments from same origin (e.g., two vendors in Guangzhou sharing one 40&#x27; HQ container), (b) balance weight and volume — pair heavy items (tiles) with light items (hardware) to maximize both weight and cube utilization, (c) identify LCL (less-than-container-load) candidates for consolidation into FCL, (d) calculate target utilization: ≥ 85% cube or ≥ 90% weight capacity
Responsible (R): Import Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1435_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1435_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1435_Task8" name="Carrier and port selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Carrier and port selection: Based on consolidation plan: (a) select carrier based on: transit time reliability, container availability at origin, Manila/Batangas port congestion forecast, freight rate competitiveness, (b) select destination port: Manila (MICT/South Harbor) for Luzon DCs; Batangas for DC3 Calamba (shorter inland transport); Cebu/Mandaue port for DC2 direct discharge if volume justifies, (c) for peak season: pre-book container space 2–3 weeks ahead to secure allocation
Responsible (R): Import Manager / Freight Forwarder
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1435_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1435_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1435_Task9" name="Carrier space confirmation and booking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Carrier space confirmation and booking: Freight forwarder confirms container allocation and booking; Import Manager validates: (a) ETD and ETA align with DC receiving capacity, (b) container type matches cargo (40&#x27; HQ for tiles, 20&#x27; GP for heavy steel), (c) transit time meets replenishment deadline; escalate to alternate carrier if primary cannot confirm within 48 hours
Responsible (R): Freight Forwarder
Accountable (A): Import Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1435_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1435_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1435_Task10" name="Port congestion monitoring and contingency">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Port congestion monitoring and contingency: Daily monitoring of target port congestion status via Philippine Ports Authority (PPA) bulletins and freight forwarder updates; if congestion exceeds 5-day dwell time: (a) activate contingency: reroute to alternate port (e.g., Subic Bay for Luzon-bound, Cebu for Visayas), (b) notify DC of delayed arrival and adjust replenishment schedules, (c) authorize overtime receiving at DC for expedited processing upon arrival
Responsible (R): Import Manager / Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1435_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1435_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1435_Task11" name="Monthly container utilization review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly container utilization review: Import Manager compiles monthly utilization report: (a) average container utilization rate (target: ≥ 85%), (b) demurrage/detention cost per container (target: &lt; PHP 15,000/container), (c) port dwell time trends, (d) per-unit freight cost by category; present to VP Supply Chain for carrier performance review and rate negotiation
Responsible (R): Import Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1435_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1435_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1435_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1435_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1435_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-245 (ensure controlled execution — Supply Chain Orchestration &amp; Risk (PA-02.3).) | - operational: Import &amp; Customs Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Import &amp; Customs Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1435_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1435_Annotation13" targetRef="W1435_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1435_Flow15" sourceRef="W1435_Start5" targetRef="W1435_Task6" />
