    <bpmn:process id="W_W1436" name="W1436. Philippine Construction Material Price Volatility Monitoring, Forward Buy Decision &amp; Cost Hedge Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly commodity price review; or significant price movement alert (&gt; 5% change in key commodity index)
Frequency: Monthly formal review; weekly price monitoring during volatile periods; ad-hoc triggered by commodity price spikes
Volume: ~15–20 key commodities monitored (steel rebar, cement, plywood, G.I. sheets, copper wire, PVC resin, ceramic tiles, paint raw materials); ~PHP 42–45B annual COGS exposure
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, Category Managers (Lumber, Plumbing, Electrical, Tiles, Paint), Purchasing Manager, Finance Controller, VP Supply Chain
Source: workflow W1436 — Philippine Construction Material Price Volatility Monitoring, Forward Buy Decision &amp; Cost Hedge Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1436_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1436_Lane1" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1436_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1436_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1436_Lane2" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1436_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1436_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1436_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1436_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1436_Lane4" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1436_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1436_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1436_Start6" name="Monthly commodity price review; or significant price movement alert (&gt; 5% change in key…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1436_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1436_Task7" name="Monthly commodity price review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly commodity price review: Category Managers compile price data for 15–20 key commodities: (a) current supplier quoted prices vs. previous month, (b) global commodity indices (LME steel, copper; Shanghai plywood index), (c) PHP/USD exchange rate trend, (d) DTI suggested retail price advisories for basic construction materials, (e) competitor pricing intelligence; present summary dashboard to VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): Category Managers
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1436_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1436_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1436_Task8" name="Price trend analysis and forecast">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Price trend analysis and forecast: VP Merchandising and Finance Controller analyze: (a) 6-month price trend for each commodity, (b) upcoming demand drivers (typhoon season, government projects, holiday construction), (c) supply-side risks (port congestion, supplier capacity constraints, import restrictions), (d) recommend forward buy decision for commodities expected to increase &gt; 5% in next 90 days
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1436_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1436_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1436_Task9" name="Forward buy authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Forward buy authorization: For recommended forward buys: (a) Category Manager calculates forward buy quantity (3–6 months supply for A-items expected to spike), (b) Finance Controller evaluates working capital impact and storage capacity at DCs, (c) VP Merchandising approves forward buy up to PHP 10M; CFO approves PHP 10–50M; CEO approves &gt; PHP 50M, (d) Purchasing Manager issues forward buy PO with negotiated price lock
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising / CFO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1436_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1436_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1436_Task10" name="Price protection pass-through analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Price protection pass-through analysis: Finance Controller and VP Merchandising evaluate whether to: (a) absorb price increase (reduce margin but maintain competitive positioning), (b) pass through to SRP (protect margin but risk price-sensitive customer defection), (c) negotiate vendor cost sharing (vendor absorbs partial increase to maintain volume), (d) implement promotional pricing to offset customer perception of price increase
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1436_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1436_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1436_Task11" name="Quarterly hedge effectiveness review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly hedge effectiveness review: VP Merchandising and Finance Controller review: (a) actual commodity prices vs. forward buy prices locked, (b) total savings (or loss) from forward buy decisions, (c) inventory carrying cost of forward-bought stock, (d) working capital tied up in forward buys, (e) adjust forward buy strategy parameters for next quarter
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1436_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1436_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1436_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1436_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1436_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-245 (ensure controlled execution — Supply Chain Orchestration &amp; Risk (PA-02.3).) | - operational: VP Merchandising review and approval gate
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
